'''/// `sorted([3, 1], strict_mode=True)` answered `[1, 3]` — the caller asked for
/// a stricter mode and silently got the default one.
///
/// **And the complaint itself moved in 3.13.** `sorted`, `print`, `int`,
/// `round`, `enumerate`, `zip`, `min`, `max`, `open` and `list.sort` all say
/// `'k' is an invalid keyword argument for f()` on 3.9 through 3.12 and
/// `f() got an unexpected keyword argument 'k'` on 3.13 — measured on
/// 3.9.23 / 3.10.20 / 3.11.15 / 3.12.3 / 3.13.12, 2026-09-12. Both halves are
